coordinating person-centered care across health, disability, and social

3043
03:02:00.686 --> 03:02:04.546
sectors. Collect information once and use it many times.

3044
03:02:05.306 --> 03:02:08.966
Insert national consistency and quality assurances to address the postcode

3045
03:02:09.006 --> 03:02:12.806
inequity that currently exists in assessment and allocation decisions.

3046
03:02:13.266 --> 03:02:16.046
Insert safeguards for people receiving paid whānau

3047
03:02:16.146 --> 03:02:19.786
care to protect disabled persons from choice and

3048
03:02:19.846 --> 03:02:20.426
control.

3049
03:02:22.326 --> 03:02:26.106
Require rights consistency for all programs and ministerial

3050
03:02:26.166 --> 03:02:30.006
directions so that protections cannot quietly be eroded between

3051
03:02:30.046 --> 03:02:33.806
elections. The disabled people and whānau that

3052
03:02:33.866 --> 03:02:37.706
NASCA organizations work with every day deserve a system that is clear, consistent,

3053
03:02:37.866 --> 03:02:41.566
safe, and rights affirming. This bill has the potential to deliver that,

3054
03:02:41.986 --> 03:02:44.266
but only if these amendments are made.

3055
03:02:45.306 --> 03:02:47.866
We urge the committee to recommend that these changes

3056
03:02:49.626 --> 03:02:53.466
are made before the bill proceeds. Happy to answer any questions.

