03:03:56.756 --> 03:04:00.436
Aotearoa. The National Māori Disabled Persons Organization

3076
03:04:00.496 --> 03:04:04.016
representing Tangata Whaikaha Māori me ō tātou whānau.

3077
03:04:05.216 --> 03:04:08.955
The question before the committee is not whether disabled people need

3078
03:04:09.176 --> 03:04:12.756
support. The question is what that support is intended to

3079
03:04:12.796 --> 03:04:13.256
achieve.

3080
03:04:14.496 --> 03:04:18.256
Our written submission sets out the legal and constitutional reasons

3081
03:04:18.336 --> 03:04:22.246
why we oppose this bill. Today, we want to focus on what

3082
03:04:22.276 --> 03:04:25.716
this bill means for the lives of disabled Māori and our whānau.

3083
03:04:26.796 --> 03:04:28.436
We've asked the committee to consider

3084
03:04:29.316 --> 03:04:30.496
one fundamental question:

3085
03:04:31.356 --> 03:04:33.636
What is the purpose of disability support?

3086
03:04:34.356 --> 03:04:36.956
For Te Ao Marama Aotearoa Trust, the answer is clear.

3087
03:04:37.596 --> 03:04:40.616
Disability support is not simply about providing care,

3088
03:04:41.456 --> 03:04:45.116
it is about enabling disabled people to participate.

3089
03:04:45.136 --> 03:04:49.016
For Tangata Whaikaha Māori, participation means being able to contribute to

3090
03:04:49.056 --> 03:04:52.536
our whānau, stand on our marae, practice our tikanga,

3091
03:04:53.096 --> 03:04:56.396
speak our reo, raise our tamariki and mokopuna,

3092
03:04:56.976 --> 03:05:00.776
work, learn, lead, and fulfill our responsibilities within our

3093
03:05:00.816 --> 03:05:03.836
hapū, iwi and communities.

3094
03:05:04.896 --> 03:05:07.436
Participation is not an optional outcome.

3095
03:05:08.876 --> 03:05:11.056
It is the purpose of disability support.

3096
03:05:11.576 --> 03:05:13.656
Yet this bill changes that purpose.

3097
03:05:14.236 --> 03:05:17.536
Instead of asking, "What support does this person need to

3098
03:05:17.636 --> 03:05:21.616
participate?" It increasingly asks, "What support can their whānau

3099
03:05:21.656 --> 03:05:23.476
provide before the Crown will?"

3100
03:05:24.676 --> 03:05:28.496
That is a profound shift. As Māori, we value whanaungatanga,

3101
03:05:29.076 --> 03:05:33.056
a whānau who have always supported one another through aroha, whakapapa

3102
03:05:33.076 --> 03:05:36.696
and collective responsibility. But our submission is clear.

3103
03:05:37.416 --> 03:05:41.326
Whānau support should be complement disability

3104
03:05:41.436 --> 03:05:45.356
support, not replace it. When the Crown assumes that

3105
03:05:45.376 --> 03:05:48.456
whānau will simply do more, disabled Māori lose

3106
03:05:48.536 --> 03:05:51.596
opportunities to participate independently.

3107
03:05:52.396 --> 03:05:53.376
Whānau lose choice.

3108
03:05:54.356 --> 03:05:57.596
Parents become carers before they can simply be parents.

3109
03:05:58.316 --> 03:06:00.076
Grandparents postpone retirement.

3110
03:06:01.016 --> 03:06:04.836
Siblings take on caring responsibilities that change family relationships.

3111
03:06:05.416 --> 03:06:08.556
And too often, wāhine Māori carry the greatest burden.

3112
03:06:09.956 --> 03:06:12.476
Whanaungatanga is one of our greatest strengths.

3113
03:06:12.536 --> 03:06:15.796
It should never become a physical infrastructure for the Crown.

3114
03:06:16.676 --> 03:06:20.266
Our submission also highlights that this bill weakens the foundation

3115
03:06:20.656 --> 03:06:22.716
that participation depends upon.

3116
03:06:23.396 --> 03:06:27.196
It removes employment protections for many family carers.

3117
03:06:27.856 --> 03:06:31.416
It removes important avenues of accountability through the Human Rights

3118
03:06:31.496 --> 03:06:33.856
Commission and the Health and Disability Commissioner.

3119
03:06:35.216 --> 03:06:38.756
It creates a legislative framework for future means testing of

3120
03:06:38.796 --> 03:06:42.596
disability support through ministerial programs rather

3121
03:06:42.716 --> 03:06:43.416
than Parliament.

3122
03:06:44.276 --> 03:06:48.136
Together, these changes reduce certainty for disabled

3123
03:06:48.216 --> 03:06:51.996
people and their whānau, while increasing ministerial discretion.

3124
03:06:52.876 --> 03:06:56.696
There is no meaningful recognition of Te Tiriti o Waitangi,

3125
03:06:57.416 --> 03:07:01.026
no recognition of the United Nations Convention on the Rights of

3126
03:07:01.116 --> 03:07:04.196
Persons with Disabilities, no recognitions of Māori

3127
03:07:04.256 --> 03:07:08.156
self-determination, and no recognition that disability supports

3128
03:07:08.216 --> 03:07:11.996
exist to enable disabled people to participate fully and

3129
03:07:12.116 --> 03:07:13.276
equally in society.

3130
03:07:14.156 --> 03:07:17.316
Te Ao Marama Trust has long supported legislation to underpin

3131
03:07:17.716 --> 03:07:21.456
disability support. But legislation must strengthen

3132
03:07:21.516 --> 03:07:24.576
rights, not weaken them. It must enable

3133
03:07:24.656 --> 03:07:28.196
participation, not increase dependency.

3134
03:07:29.016 --> 03:07:32.216
It must support whānau, not shift the Crown's

3135
03:07:32.276 --> 03:07:36.246
responsibilities onto them, and it must be developed with

3136
03:07:36.276 --> 03:07:38.706
disabled people, not without them.

3137
03:07:39.416 --> 03:07:43.155
For these reasons, our recommendation remains unchanged.

3138
03:07:43.196 --> 03:07:46.876
We respectfully ask the committee to recommend that this

3139
03:07:46.916 --> 03:07:50.706
bill does not proceed, and that the new legislative framework be

3140
03:07:50.856 --> 03:07:53.836
co-designed with disabled people and their representative

3141
03:07:53.876 --> 03:07:56.216
organizations from the beginning.

3142
03:07:56.876 --> 03:07:58.536
We leave you with this final thought.

3143
03:07:59.096 --> 03:08:02.956
The measure of a disability support system is not how much care it

3144
03:08:02.966 --> 03:08:06.636
provides. The true measure is whether disabled people can

3145
03:08:06.676 --> 03:08:10.636
participate fully in the lives they choose alongside their whānau, their

3146
03:08:10.676 --> 03:08:14.616
communities, and their culture. No reira, ngā mihi atu

3147
03:08:14.816 --> 03:08:17.226
kia koutou, tēnā koutou, tēnā koutou.

3148
03:08:18.476 --> 03:08:19.996
