with great complexity, Chair of the NZDSN Disability Support

3181
03:09:52.304 --> 03:09:55.904
Network, and Chief Executive for the Supported Lifestyle Hauraki Trust.

3182
03:09:56.864 --> 03:10:00.284
We support disabled people to live full lives in their communities with dignity,

3183
03:10:00.384 --> 03:10:02.364
independence, participation, and choice.

3184
03:10:03.104 --> 03:10:06.904
We also work within the disability support services system every day, giving us

3185
03:10:06.924 --> 03:10:10.794
practical insight into both the benefits of the system and the challenges it

3186
03:10:10.844 --> 03:10:14.664
currently faces. We support the government's objective of creating a more

3187
03:10:14.704 --> 03:10:18.684
accountable and sustainable disability support system, and we recognize

3188
03:10:18.704 --> 03:10:22.484
the pressures on public funding and understand the need for clear legislative

3189
03:10:22.584 --> 03:10:26.424
foundations. However, if there is one message I would like the committee to

3190
03:10:26.464 --> 03:10:28.984
take away for our submission today, it is this.

3191
03:10:29.444 --> 03:10:33.324
The long-term success of this bill will depend less on what

3192
03:10:33.364 --> 03:10:37.344
it enables government to do, and more on whether disabled people and their families

3193
03:10:37.424 --> 03:10:37.784
trust it.

3194
03:10:39.224 --> 03:10:42.644
The concerns we're hearing across the sector are not primarily about today's

3195
03:10:42.684 --> 03:10:46.124
funding levels. They are about confidence in the future.

3196
03:10:46.184 --> 03:10:49.144
Many people are concerned that significant powers are being created without

3197
03:10:49.184 --> 03:10:52.104
sufficient safeguards around how they may be exercised by future

3198
03:10:52.144 --> 03:10:56.024
governments. Our submission, therefore, focuses

3199
03:10:56.064 --> 03:10:59.864
on building trust through a small number of practical amendments.

3200
03:10:59.904 --> 03:11:03.484
The first is ensuring that the major future changes are subject to public

3201
03:11:03.504 --> 03:11:05.604
consultation and parliamentary scrutiny.

3202
03:11:06.244 --> 03:11:10.014
Significant changes to the lives of disabled people should be transparent and

3203
03:11:10.104 --> 03:11:11.944
subject to democratic oversight.

3204
03:11:12.884 --> 03:11:15.784
The second relates to families, and I know you've heard a lot of this feedback

3205
03:11:15.824 --> 03:11:16.144
already.

3206
03:11:17.044 --> 03:11:21.024
Families provide extraordinary support to disabled New Zealanders, but

3207
03:11:21.104 --> 03:11:23.804
families vary greatly in their capacity to do so.

3208
03:11:24.444 --> 03:11:28.344
We therefore believe the legislation should make it clear that family support may

3209
03:11:28.384 --> 03:11:30.824
be considered but never be presumed.

3210
03:11:31.444 --> 03:11:35.204
Support should only be taken into account where family members are both willing and

3211
03:11:35.304 --> 03:11:39.114
able to provide it. We also wish to comment specifically on

3212
03:11:39.144 --> 03:11:41.544
the family employment provisions.

3213
03:11:41.584 --> 03:11:45.264
We understand the desire to clarify the legal status of family carers and the

3214
03:11:45.304 --> 03:11:48.834
Crown. However, we would encourage the committee to consider whether this

3215
03:11:48.844 --> 03:11:52.824
component of the bill could be separated from the broader disability support

3216
03:11:52.904 --> 03:11:55.844
services framework and addressed through a more focused

3217
03:11:55.884 --> 03:11:59.874
process. The issues surrounding family employment are complex and

3218
03:11:59.904 --> 03:12:03.104
important in their own right. They raise different policy

3219
03:12:03.114 --> 03:12:07.084
considerations from those relating to the overall governance and operation

3220
03:12:07.124 --> 03:12:10.844
of disability support services. Separating these issues may allow both

3221
03:12:10.924 --> 03:12:14.624
areas to receive the level of attention they deserve without

3222
03:12:15.444 --> 03:12:18.374
creating unnecessary complexity within the primary legislation.

3223
03:12:20.124 --> 03:12:24.004
More broadly, we would also urge caution against attempting to solve every

3224
03:12:24.064 --> 03:12:26.264
concern through additional legislative prescription.

3225
03:12:27.004 --> 03:12:30.763
While safeguards are important, there is a risk that the legislation becomes

3226
03:12:30.904 --> 03:12:34.453
so detailed, so heavily qualified, and so constrained by

3227
03:12:34.504 --> 03:12:38.324
amendments that it creates a system that is inflexible and difficult to

3228
03:12:38.364 --> 03:12:40.824
operate, which is how the system was

3229
03:12:40.844 --> 03:12:44.694
previously. One of the reasons reforms have been pursued is

3230
03:12:44.704 --> 03:12:48.404
because previous arrangements were often seen as complex, difficult to navigate,

3231
03:12:48.444 --> 03:12:51.024
and challenging to administer consistently.

3232
03:12:51.064 --> 03:12:54.564
We should be careful not to replace one set of problems with another.

3233
03:12:54.584 --> 03:12:57.894
The challenge is finding the right balance, providing appropriate protections and

3234
03:12:57.964 --> 03:13:01.764
accountability while still allowing the system enough flexibility to respond to

3235
03:13:01.824 --> 03:13:04.664
individual circumstances and changing needs.

3236
03:13:04.744 --> 03:13:08.144
Finally, I would like to highlight what we believe is the single most important

3237
03:13:08.164 --> 03:13:11.244
recommendation in our submission.

3238
03:13:11.284 --> 03:13:14.644
Regardless of how carefully legislation is drafted, disagreements will

3239
03:13:14.664 --> 03:13:18.233
occur. Assessment decisions will be challenged, funding decisions will

3240
03:13:18.264 --> 03:13:21.144
sometimes be disputed, and mistakes will inevitably happen.

3241
03:13:22.004 --> 03:13:25.884
For that reason, we strongly support the establishment of an independent review and

3242
03:13:25.944 --> 03:13:29.864
appeals mechanism. An independent disability support review tribunal

3243
03:13:29.904 --> 03:13:33.624
or something similar would provide confidence that decisions can be reviewed

3244
03:13:33.684 --> 03:13:36.324
fairly, transparently, and independently.

3245
03:13:36.404 --> 03:13:39.624
Importantly, such a mechanism does not guarantee increased

3246
03:13:39.664 --> 03:13:42.164
spending. It guarantees accountability.

3247
03:13:42.744 --> 03:13:46.544
In our view, no other amendment would do more to strengthen trust in the system.

3248
03:13:47.464 --> 03:13:50.624
In closing, we support the intent of the bill and recognize the need for

3249
03:13:50.664 --> 03:13:52.764
sustainable disability support services.

3250
03:13:53.344 --> 03:13:56.844
Our recommendations are intended to achieve three things: maintain trust,

3251
03:13:57.184 --> 03:14:00.544
protect the rights of disabled people and their families, and preserve sufficient

3252
03:14:00.584 --> 03:14:03.864
flexibility for the system to operate effectively in practice.

3253
03:14:04.764 --> 03:14:07.364
Thank you for the opportunity to appear before you today.

3254
03:14:08.704 --> 03:14:11.744
Thank you very much, Samantha. And thanks for bringing a new

3255
03:14:12.684 --> 03:14:14.024
proposal which we haven't heard yet.

